# Build-context exclusions for BOTH images built from this repo root:
# Dockerfile (backend, whose final `COPY . .` takes everything not listed here)
# and docker/dashboard/Dockerfile. Measured in CI: that COPY layer was 233 MB
# and is now 14.6 MB — almost none of it was needed at runtime, and because the
# context changes on every commit, it also invalidated the layer cache
# constantly.
#
# This is a DENYLIST on purpose. An allowlist would silently drop a new
# directory the runtime needs; here the failure mode of forgetting an entry is
# a slightly larger image, not a broken one. Before adding a line, check it is
# not needed by either Dockerfile — the dashboard build copies
# `olano/dashboard_2.0/` and `assets/`, and the backend serves the WhatsApp
# bridge from `whatsapp-bridge/` (runtime/api.py runs `npm install` in it).

# ── version control ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ~80 MB in CI, and every commit changes it, so it busts the cache too.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# ── tests + dev tooling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The image runs the product, not the suite (19 MB).
tests/
.claude/
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# ── the native mobile app ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# mobile/ is the Capacitor shell built for the App Store and Google Play; it
# loads a deployment's dashboard over the network and nothing in either image
# reads it. Its native projects (Gradle, Xcode) are large and change often.
mobile/

# ── demo videos ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# demo/ records the product films (scripts, voiceover MP3s, a chart). Nothing
# in either image reads it, and `COPY . .` would otherwise put several MB of
# audio into every runtime image.
demo/

# ── dev/test agent fixtures ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The repo-local agents/ dir holds only internal per-provider test agents
# (test-agent-*, test-monetization-agent). Customer images must not contain
# them at all — the loader additionally refuses the project-local dir on
# managed deployments (olano/config/loader.py). Dev containers keep them via
# the docker-compose.yml bind mount (./agents:/app/agents:ro).
agents/

# ── caches and build outputs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# node_modules is rebuilt by `npm ci` inside the dashboard build; shipping the
# host's copy would both bloat the context and risk platform-specific binaries.
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.venv
venv/
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info

# ── local state that must never enter an image ───────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
.olano-tester/
.DS_Store
